    "body": "This adds `research/tensor-response-r715/`, a source-bound offline construction and replay package.\n\n**Conditional kappa = 0.001296606691405309**, exactly `1296606691405309/1000000000000000000`: **+0.08476450% over #478** (`0.001295508560071773`) and **+0.19840410% over the pinned warm #473 claim** (`0.001294039264416565`). The bit supplier binds. This compares the complete whole-owner route; it is not a claim to exceed proposals using different admission assumptions.\n\n## Concrete new mechanisms\n\n1. **Simultaneous response-kernel cancellation.** Compute each immutable-source injection's transported target response. Delete a packet only when its response sum vanishes for every source. The useful cross-helper pair reads source3 at helpers444 and246; neither injection is removable alone. Rebuild inverse cleanup. Its local paid delta replaces rank1 plus rank5 by rank6, so strict subadditivity gives a moment improvement for every relevant exponent. Ten further duplicate pairs only reduce scalar work. Altogether22 injections and22 cleanup additions disappear, with all22 single-deletion controls rejected.\n2. **Nested-donor flags.** Replace the old one-entrance-per-donor construction restriction with an explicit sufficient flag schedule. Donors receive logical shears at increasing nested frames; all dirty values remain arbitrary. Ten pivot upgrades yield110 pivots,102 physical donors,120 correction groups and total entrance rank129. Exact response relations, frame chains and residual isometries are checked. The new constructor is explicit; the old constructor's equal-entrance guard is not silently ignored.\n\nThese are combined with the new retain-and-repair #473 kernel and our14 target factors from #478. Gains are priced through the complete composed program, never added. The full local/native and physical ownership checks use the actual changed word. All88 calls use one uniform provider; all62920 residual occurrences remain wholly on single physical families. No unverified heterogeneous portfolio or cross-family split contributes.\n\n## Exact pricing and validation\n\n- Bit saving lower bound: `1298290062988365072981/1000000000000000000000000`.\n- Complex saving lower bound: `1305231506267591/1000000000000000000`, the unchanged source-bound completed supplier from #471.\n- Bit dimension78,9600 live/9609 physical families; complete rank mass745536.\n- Fresh physical prefix837bits, charged896; three-level coefficient2567bits, charged2624; row coefficient19431<20161.\n- Source reconstruction,955 arbitrary-dirty binary columns, rational frames/integer operand spans, native signed/formal columns, physical target labels, mixing controls, Gram/projectors, global owner audit, fresh invoice, both exact moment implementations and all47 strict outer inequalities pass. Mutation controls cover the changed constructors and inherited physical audit.\n\nRun:\n\n```text\npython -B research/tensor-response-r715/verify.py /absolute/new/output\n```\n\nPython3.11+, SymPy, a C++17 compiler and Boost headers are required. Replay uses no network or optimizer. Default replay rebuilds both suppliers. Our completed changed-component run explicitly reuses the unchanged complex supplier only after matching87 implementation hashes and17 output hashes against its pinned completed receipt. That mode emits a distinct receipt; it is not described as a fresh complex execution. VALIDATION.json records the actual run scope. GitHub CI is separate and is not claimed passed.\n\n## Sources, credit and retained research\n\nDirect inputs: #473 (new warm kernel), #478 (retained14 target factors), #472/#470/#467 (R715 kernels, retiming, whole-owner pooling), #463 (R715 carrier and XOR word), #450 (target mixing), #455/#476 (earlier target factoring and portable audits), and #471 (unchanged complex normalization/spectators). The retained complex/hosting/compiler lineage includes #449, #456, #457, #451, #454, #417, #442, #433, #425, #386, #377 and #370; outer